From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@t1100.local>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:01:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: enable the MT6370 DSV rails for the panel

The panel is powered from the MT6370 sub-PMIC: VPOS/VNEG are the DSV
outputs (stock DT: mt6370_pmu_dsv, mt6370_dsvp/dsvn with a 6 V ceiling,
db_vbst = 0x1644 = 5700 mV). Without them the 1600x2176 panel stays
dark no matter what the DSI side does.

Enable the MFD node only. It keeps the ADC child and the regulators
block that were already described, and deliberately has no charger,
TCPC, flashlight or indicator child: mt6370_probe() creates a platform
device per MFD_CELL_OF only when the matching child node exists, so the
Type-C controller (which the vendor tree uses to drive VBUS and the USB
role, and which would fight the RNDIS port this port depends on) is
simply never instantiated. The driver still needs the EINT: probe calls
devm_regmap_add_irq_chip() with i2c->irq, hence
interrupts-extended = <&pio 10 ...>, the same pin the mt6771-next port
of the same board uses.

MT6370 (MFD + regulator, drivers/mfd/mt6370.c and
drivers/regulator/mt6370-regulator.c) exist in 6.12; the gate bit
comment in the port notes applies to the DISP power domain, not to this
PMIC.

To verify on hardware: "mt6370-regulator mt6370-regulator.0: Failed to
register (N) regulator" and the i2c5 probe of 0x34 must both be absent,
and regulator_summary must show mt6370-dsv-vpos/vneg enabled while the
panel is on.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index 926ee0558..bfd2b21ad 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -263,7 +263,7 @@ &i2c5 {
 	pmic@34 {
 		compatible = "mediatek,mt6370";
 		reg = <0x34>;
-		status = "disabled";
+		wakeup-source;
 
 		interrupts-extended = <&pio 10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		interrupt-controller;
